# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]   (no dollar/backtick in the text)
register_gate "tests/test_marketplace_billing_off.py" "MARKETPLACE BILLING OFF GATE: PASS" "marketplace billing off" "marketplace billing OFF by default (economic-security P1: the future GitHub-Marketplace billing path -- the marketplace_purchase handler that can write a Core plan via core.set_account_plan_with_authority -- is gated behind VERIPSA_MARKETPLACE_BILLING and DEFAULTS OFF, so a free-first Marketplace listing cannot mint paid Core access before platform entitlement sync, purchase events, and payer-org binding are implemented. Proves OFFLINE [recording fake db, no Postgres] that with the flag OFF/unset a marketplace_purchase 'purchased' event -- and every action purchased/changed/cancelled/pending_change -- is a content-free NOOP: core.set_account_plan_* is NEVER called and the result is an honest skipped/noop dict; only the exact string '1' arms it ['','0','true' read OFF, no accidental enable]; with the flag ON the existing future seam is preserved [purchased DOES call the gated plan setter with the resolved account id + plan label, cancelled writes 'free']; the handler body is KEPT INTACT for a possible future Marketplace SKU and carries the reconcile-before-enable note [enabling it REQUIRES writing the platform entitlement tables + binding payer-org].)" "marketplace billing OFF by default (the marketplace_purchase -> set_account_plan path is INERT unless VERIPSA_MARKETPLACE_BILLING=1; future paid Marketplace requires entitlement sync and payer-org binding first; SECURITY-critical -- it governs the free-first quota wall)" 24
